<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Mozambique gets $36 million for road improvement.</title>
<headline>Mozambique gets $36 million for road improvement.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The African Development Bank (AfDB) said on Wednesday that it was lending Mozambique $36 million to improve a 210-km (130-mile) road used to transport cash crops from Montepuez to the coastal town of Pemba.</p>
<p>The money will come from its soft loan arm, the African Development Fund, and like all such loans will be repayable over 50 years with 10 years grace.</p>
<p>The bank said the money will finance all the foreign currency costs of the project and 21 percent of the local currency costs, representing 90 percent of the total cost of the work.</p>
</text>
